-- erwartet: R013
-- **Poison 607 -- the RIGHTS half of a pointer declaration, which nothing read.**
--
-- `R008` was built on 2026-08-24 out of the pass register's finding that the address space
-- was checked nowhere. It reads `TypExpr::Zeiger(z).raum` and stops there. **`z.rechte` sits
-- in the same struct, two fields down, and no line compared it at a call.**
--
-- Measured 2026-09-02 against the unchanged checker: this file gave **0 errors, 0 hints**.
-- The emitter is faithful and writes what the declaration says --
--
--     static void schreibt(Text *restrict p);
--     static void ruft(const Text *restrict q) { schreibt(q); }
--
-- -- and `cc -Werror` refuses it: *passing argument 1 of 'schreibt' discards 'const'
-- qualifier from pointer target type*. **The `N041` shape: the checker confirms and the
-- foreign compiler is what holds the line.**
--
-- ## And the direction is the whole rule
--
-- Unlike the address space, rights are NOT symmetric. `R008` asks `ist != soll` and is right
-- to -- there is no lattice over `mmio` and `normal`, they are simply different memories.
-- Rights have one:
--
--   * `rw` at an `r` parameter is NARROWING and legitimate. The callee promises to do less
--     than it could. `crates/gabbro-check/tests/gestalt.rs` already pinned that row before
--     this rule existed (*a wider right at a narrower slot*), and it must stay silent.
--   * `r` at an `rw` parameter -- this file -- is the unsound one.
--
-- **The counter-direction cannot live in this directory** -- a file here must fall -- so it
-- stands as a speech test: `tests/rechte.rs::ein_engerer_slot_bleibt_still`, and
-- `tests/gestalt.rs` had the row before this rule existed.

module gift::pointer_rights_widen_at_a_call {

type Text = { n : u32, };

impl fn schreibt(p : ptr<normal, rw> Text)
    effects { writes p }
    costs   <= 4 ops
{
    p.n = 1;
}

impl fn ruft(q : ptr<normal, r> Text)
    effects { writes q }
    costs   <= 8 ops
{
    schreibt(q);
}

}
